    <step order="6" name="Checkpoint (after 3 rows)">Run `context-handoff` + `az bicep build` dry-run on modified files.</step>
    <step order="7" name="A13 apply">Add Service Bus Data Receiver role assignment for L2 UAMI on SB namespace via `platform-controlplane.bicep` (or dedicated role-assignments module).</step>
    <step order="8" name="A19 apply (3 role assignments)">Add L2 UAMI sub Contributor + Storage Blob Data Reader on artifacts storage (from A17) + AcrPull on ACR (from A18).</step>
    <step order="9" name="A20 apply (H4-shared 5-6 role assignments)">Add UAMI role assignments on shared source services per row A20: Cognitive Services User × 2 (OpenAI + DocIntel), Search Service Contributor, SB Data Owner, Storage Contributor, Redis Cache Contributor.</step>
    <step order="10" name="A21 apply (Website Contributor on BFF App Service)">Add L2 UAMI Website Contributor role assignment on target BFF App Service (enables Kudu docker-log fetch).</step>
    <step order="11" name="Checkpoint (after 4 rows)">Run `context-handoff` + `az bicep build` dry-run.</step>
    <step order="12" name="A22 apply — FromBicepOutput KV wire-up (choose approach)">CHOOSE ONE of the 3 A22 approaches; document choice + rejected alternatives per CLAUDE.md §6.5. Implement the chosen approach. Regression-check: H4 must NOT quarantine a fresh customer after this change (validate via unit test if available, otherwise document manual test recipe).</step>
    <step order="13" name="A23 apply — kv-secrets.generated.bicep skip-if-exists fix">Rewrite the unconditional ternary in `kv-secrets.generated.bicep` to genuinely skip when the secret exists (using `existing` keyword + conditional resource declaration). BEFORE + AFTER: confirm BFF-API-ClientSecret + Dataverse-ClientSecret survive a re-deploy (via `az bicep what-if` or unit test).</step>
    <step order="14" name="A25 apply (sharedBffUami KV Secrets User)">Add KV Secrets User grant to `sharedBffUami` in `model1-shared.bicep`. Confirm Model 2 `customer.bicep` unaffected.</step>
    <step order="15" name="Checkpoint (after 3 rows)">Run `context-handoff` + `az bicep build` dry-run.</step>
    <step order="16" name="A26 apply — queue-recreate ceremony">Execute `notes/queue-recreate-runbook-2026-08.md` against dev L2 stamp. Verify post-recreate queue properties via `az servicebus queue show`: `requiresSession=true` + `requiresDuplicateDetection=true`. Update runbook execution log within the runbook file.</step>
    <step order="17" name="A27 apply — CustomerRunGuard config">Add `CustomerRunGuard` config (TargetDataverseUrl / TenantId / ClientId / ClientSecret / Enabled=true) via bicep app-settings + KV secret bindings. Verify I5 serialization enforced at runtime (via unit test if available).</step>
    <step order="18" name="Build sanity">Run `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` — must succeed. Run `az bicep build` on ALL modified/new bicep files — must all succeed.</step>
    <step order="19" name="Amend punch list annotations">EDIT `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` — add `last_known_status_after_execution: applied|already-applied|deferred-because-X` per in-scope row A13..A27. Append §203b execution results subsection with any A22 approach-choice decision + A26 execution log summary.</step>
    <step order="20" name="Report">Emit concise summary: rows applied, rows already-applied, rows deferred (with reason), bicep dry-run results, dotnet build result, A22 approach chosen, A26 queue-recreate outcome, NFR-01 non-applicability confirmed (zero BFF touch). Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</step>
